  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the public disclosure doctrine is a red herring because it is designed to avoid parasitic lawsuits where information is in the public domain."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0002-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 44,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, eRISA contains a retaliatory discharge provision, and courts have consistently held that there is no express limitations period for it, so the most analogous state law\u2019s limitations period must be applied."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christopher G. Browning, Jr.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christopher G. Browning, Jr., according to Christopher G. Browning, Jr., the issue in this case is whether Congress expressly provided for a limitations period for retaliatory discharge action under the Federal False Claims Act."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Christopher G. Browning, Jr.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christopher G. Browning, Jr., according to Christopher G. Browning, Jr., the retaliatory discharge provision, section\u202f3730(h) of the False Claims Act, protects both the initial whistleblower and those who testify at trial."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, a retaliation claim is a civil action under section\u202f3730 and is subject to a six\u2011year limitations period."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, the limitations period should start when the litigant believes the violation occurred, i.e., based on the mental impression of the plaintiff."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0fd3acd3905183267b9a327fdc43f1bbff42a486d63308fef30bc7e4da84ff6c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0fd3acd39051-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, having the same trigger for all three 3730 actions means the limitations period starts for all three at the same time, making it easier for the whistleblower to bring both qui tam and retaliation actions together."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent",
      "status": "complete",
